{
  "duration": 91.719,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.959,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.5,
      "end": 4.259,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem. Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.859,
      "end": 5.699,
      "text": "tan theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.539,
      "end": 8.439,
      "text": "is equal to seven by twenty-four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.0,
      "end": 9.559,
      "text": "and theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.0,
      "end": 11.3,
      "text": "is an acute angle."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.699,
      "end": 12.399,
      "text": "We need to find"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.899,
      "end": 14.0,
      "text": "sec theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.779,
      "end": 18.219,
      "text": "We know that tan theta is perpendicular divided by base."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.699,
      "end": 18.819,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.239,
      "end": 20.239,
      "text": "when tan theta is"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.6,
      "end": 21.5,
      "text": "seven by twenty-four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.92,
      "end": 26.199,
      "text": "we can take the perpendicular as seven and the base as twenty-four."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.68,
      "end": 28.579,
      "text": "Do these have to be the actual side lengths?"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.159,
      "end": 29.359,
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.019,
      "end": 32.139,
      "text": "Since tan gives us a ratio,"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.54,
      "end": 35.219,
      "text": "we can take any sides in the same ratio."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.739,
      "end": 38.5,
      "text": "Taking seven and twenty-four simply makes our calculation easy."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.079,
      "end": 42.02,
      "text": "We now know two sides of the right triangle, but sec theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.52,
      "end": 44.579,
      "text": "needs the hypotenuse and the base."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.02,
      "end": 47.479,
      "text": "So first, we need to find the hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.0,
      "end": 55.439,
      "text": "Using the Pythagoras theorem, hypotenuse is equal to the square root of perpendicular square plus base square."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.979,
      "end": 69.299,
      "text": "Putting the values, we get the square root of seven square plus twenty-four square. This becomes the square root of forty-nine plus five hundred seventy-six, which is the square root of six hundred twenty-five."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.879,
      "end": 75.259,
      "text": "So the hypotenuse is twenty-five. Now, sec theta is hypotenuse divided by base."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.879,
      "end": 76.4,
      "text": "Therefore,"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.819,
      "end": 83.58,
      "text": "sec theta is twenty-five by twenty-four. Since theta is an acute angle, we take the positive value."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.339,
      "end": 84.779,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.479,
      "end": 91.719,
      "text": "sec theta is twenty-five by twenty-four. So the correct option is C."
    }
  ],
